  "conclusions": [
    "The sharp sub-eV in-plane loss features in Graphene-BC3 and Graphene-B4C3 are distinct from the approximately 2 and 5 eV negative-real-dielectric-response features discussed for Graphene-Borophene.",
    "Graphene-Borophene has no corresponding sub-eV local loss peak under the stated peak-selection settings; it does have broader loss features at higher energies.",
    "The three dominant out-of-plane loss peaks lie at approximately 17.88, 18.08 and 18.61 eV, within the approximate 17--19 eV description.",
    "Graphene-Borophene is not the strongest absorber over the full displayed spectrum; a claim of stronger absorption must be restricted to the low-energy onset region.",
    "Graphene-BC3 epsilon1_xx is not positive over the entire plotted energy range; small negative intervals are present."
  ]
